:: ===========================================================================
:: breaking.sca — stress- and cluster-conditioned sound changes for SCArs.
::
:: Demonstrates that the SCArs rule language expresses prosodic context, not just
:: flat segmental rewrites. Stress is written with an acute accent on the vowel
:: (á é í ó ú). A syllable is treated as OPEN when the stressed vowel is followed
:: by a single consonant and then a vowel (… V́ C V …); the breaking rules fire
:: only there, so the same vowel before a consonant CLUSTER (a closed syllable)
:: is left untouched — i.e. the change is both stress- and cluster-conditioned.
::
:: Apply with:   latte sca --file lib/breaking.sca <word>..
:: ===========================================================================

class V = a e i o u ā ē ī ō ū
class C = p t k b d g m n r l s h v w j ɣ

:: --- Phase VI: stressed-vowel breaking in OPEN syllables (single C then V) ---
á > a o / _ C V
é > e a / _ C V
ó > u o / _ C V

:: --- a cluster-conditioned onset rule: s is lost before a word-initial stop ---
s > / # _ C
